── General
?        help                                                       
:        command palette                                            
q        close, or quit at the root                                 
esc      back out one level                                         
ctrl+c   cancel the running command, else quit                      
u        undo                                                       jj undo
ctrl+r   redo                                                       jj redo
ctrl+l   reload from the source                                     jj log
tab      next pane                                                  
!        shell in the repository root                               
K        what is this                                               jj log -r <rev> -T ...
Y        yank a reference                                           
gm       messages and the last failure                              
── Move
gg       top                                                        
G        bottom                                                     
j/down   down a line                                                
k/up     up a line                                                  
ctrl+d   half a page down                                           
ctrl+u   half a page up                                             
@        jump to the working copy                                   
── Find
/        search                                                     
── Read
U        only what is unread                                        
H        choose the round to compare against                        jj evolog -r <rev>
I        outline                                                    jj log -r 'trunk()..<rev> | <rev>:: ~ ::trunk()'
── Jump
]u       next unread                                                
[u       previous unread                                            
]r       next round                                                 jj interdiff --from <a> --to <b>
[r       previous round                                             jj interdiff --from <a> --to <b>
── Look
enter    diff the revision                                          jj diff -r <rev>
p        dock the diff beside the log, following the cursor         jj diff -r <rev> --git
l        files in the revision                                      jj diff -r <rev> --summary
=        diff against another revision                              jj diff --from <a> --to <b>
── Rewrite
n        new on the revision (two or more checked: a merge)         jj new <revs>
e        edit                                                       jj edit <rev>
E        edit the revision's content in the diff editor             jj diffedit -r <rev>
d        describe                                                   jj describe -r <rev> -m <message>
D        describe in $EDITOR                                        jj describe -r <rev>
c        commit @: describe it and start a new one                  jj commit -m <message>
S        split into commits, one column each, in jj-diff            jj-diff --split -r <rev>
a        abandon                                                    jj abandon <revs>
A        absorb into the revisions that last touched each line      jj absorb -r <rev>
x        resolve the conflict, side by side in jj-diff              jj-diff --resolve -r <rev>
X        converge divergent changes                                 jj converge [-r change_id(<rev>)]
|        parallelize the checked revisions                          jj parallelize <revs>
space    check for a batch action                                   
B        bisect between the two checked revisions                   jj bisect run --range <a>::<b>
── Pick where it goes
N        new, choosing where it goes                                jj new -o/-A/-B <dest>
s        squash, choosing where into                                jj squash --from <rev> --into <dest>
y        duplicate, choosing where (enter: in place)                jj duplicate <rev> [-o/-A/-B <dest>]
r        rebase, choosing where                                     jj rebase -r <rev> -o <dest>
R        restore content from another revision (the parent: discard) jj restore --from <src> --into <rev>
── Repository
o        op log, with the log as it stood at each operation         jj op log
[o       the log one operation back, read-only                      jj log --at-op <op> --ignore-working-copy
]o       the log one operation forward                              jj log --at-op <op> --ignore-working-copy
f        fetch                                                      jj git fetch --all-remotes
P        push the revision's bookmarks                              jj git push -r <revs>
bb       bookmarks: the list                                        jj bookmark list
bc       create a bookmark here                                     jj bookmark create <name> -r <rev>
L        edit the revset                                            jj log -r <revset>
gh       forge pane: pull requests and CI                           
gw       workspaces                                                 jj workspace list
